=\"610\" y1=\"221.4\" y2=\"221.4\" stroke=\"#1B8FA8\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"225.4\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1B8FA8\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$194.07</tspan> 38.2% retrace</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"255.3\" y2=\"255.3\" stroke=\"#A63A2E\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"259.3\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#A63A2E\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$185.00</tspan> put idea stop</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"330.2\" y2=\"330.2\" stroke=\"#2F6E4A\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"334.2\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#2F6E4A\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$165.00</tspan> put trigger</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"362.6\" y2=\"362.6\" stroke=\"#2F6E4A\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"366.6\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#2F6E4A\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$156.34</tspan> put target 1</text><circle cx=\"515.1\" cy=\"294.5\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#C9A84C\" stroke=\"#20242C\" stroke-width=\"1\"/></svg></figure>\n<ul><li>The averages and retracement lines here are mine, not yours. The put trigger, stop and target come from the scorecard.</li><li><strong>Trend:</strong> Down. The last close of $174.54 is below the 20-day ($179.44), 50-day ($190.34) and 200-day ($213.99), and the 50-day is below the 200-day.</li><li><strong>Momentum:</strong> RSI 40.9, weak but not washed out.</li><li><strong>Ceiling:</strong> The 20-day at $179.44 and the $179 to $181.50 zone, then $185, then my 38.2% retracement of the Aug to Oct drop at $194.07. The 200-day is at $213.99.</li><li><strong>Floor:</strong> The 52-week low of $165.01, set Oct 28, the day after the report. Below it, the scorecard targets at $156.34 and $147.61. It closed $172.38, $173.38 and $174.54 on Nov 9 to 11.</li><li><strong>Your tested edge:</strong> Does not apply. This is a downtrend, your &quot;downtrend plus RSI over 60&quot; put setup has only worked on TSLA, and RSI is 40.9 anyway.</li><li><strong>Watching play:</strong> Dec 18 $170 put. Trigger: below $165 intraday, or a failed rally into $179 to $181.50. Exit above $185. The 10-day no-trade limit falls on Nov 20.</li><li><strong>Verdict:</strong> The chart supports the downside. A daily close above $185 would flip it to no lean. It agrees with what management said about cash and production, and disagrees with the record backlog.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>A daily close above $185, or a break below $165.</li><li>Proof the 737 line holds 47 a month, or any slip in 777X certification past mid-2027.</li><li>Formal 2027 detail, which management said comes in January (next report date not found).</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>High on results and backlog (release read twice). Medium-high on the cash path and rate plans (machine transcript, read twice). Prior cash flow targets were not verified. Delivery counts and certification dates come from Leeham News, not a Boeing page.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://boeing.mediaroom.com/2026-10-27-Boeing-Reports-Third-Quarter-Results\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Boeing release</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.webull.com/news/15820938356535296\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Call transcript (Webull)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.boeing.com/features/2026/09/ceo-737-10-certification-very-soon-more-to-do-to-stabilize-production\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Boeing feature, September</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.newsquawk.com/headlines/boeing-company-ba-q3-2026-usd-adj-eps--034-exp--025-revenue-242bln-exp-239bln\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Newsquawk (consensus)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://leehamnews.com/2026/10/27/wings-still-pacing-boeings-737-max-production-rate-increases/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Leeham News on wings</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.aviationpros.co